{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T11:44:35Z","timestamp":1792583075291,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":56,"publisher":"Wiley","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792540800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792540800000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["52173160"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["52173160"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Small"],"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Solar\u2010driven interfacial evaporation is a promising solution to freshwater scarcity, yet it faces bottlenecks regarding salt accumulation, limited evaporation modes, and single functionality. Here, inspired by plant vascular tissues, we have developed a 3D core\u2013shell Janus hydrogel evaporator to achieve the synergy of high\u2010efficiency freshwater production and stable hydrovoltaic energy harvesting. To construct this core\u2013shell architecture, an alkali\u2010induced dehydroflurination strategy is employed to solve the bonding challenge between hydrophobic poly(vinylidene fluoride) (PVDF) and the hydrophilic sodium alginate (SA) core, while simultaneously triggering the in situ oxidation of manganese ions to form MnO\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    , thus conferring antibacterial activity on the device. The PVA\/chitosan shell and sodium alginate core are endowed with bio\u2010inspired vascular channels through a foaming and freeze\u2010thawing process, which ensures efficient water transport and salt resistance. Crucially, this design leverages the tunable water\u2010content environment within the hydrogel and the water\u2010polymer interactions to enable a unique \u201cHydrogel\/Janus dual\u2010core\u201d evaporation mechanism. Furthermore, the incorporation of dodecasodium phytate markedly enhances the surface charge density, yielding an evaporation rate of 4.22\u00a0kg m\n                    <jats:sup>\u2212<\/jats:sup>\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    h\n                    <jats:sup>\u2212<\/jats:sup>\n                    <jats:sup>1<\/jats:sup>\n                    under one sun and a sustained output voltage of 825\u00a0mV in seawater. This bioinspired all\u2010in\u2010one platform offers a pathway from passive solar distillation to active water\u2010energy synergy.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/smll.76416","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T11:20:13Z","timestamp":1792581613000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Plant\u2010Stem\u2010Inspired Core\u2013Shell Janus Hydrogel Evaporator for Synergistic Solar Desalination and Hydrovoltaic Generation"],"prefix":"10.1002","author":[{"given":"Jiahong","family":"Gao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Chemical Engineering and Materials Heilongjiang University  Harbin People's Republic of China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Junhuan","family":"Sun","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Chemical Engineering and Materials Heilongjiang University  Harbin People's Republic of China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Huixin","fa